  "criterion": "per bare CFF program, fontTools 4.66.1 (cffLib, every glyph drawn through DecomposingRecordingPen) and fonts fontCffProgram.readCff give the same number of glyphs, per glyph index the same name (cid%05d for a CID, .notdef for its glyph 0; a .<n> suffix cffLib adds to a duplicate name is no difference), the same advance and the same moveTo / lineTo / curveTo / closePath commands at 1/1000 unit, and for a name-keyed font the same 256 built-in encoding slots (.notdef an empty slot; ExpertEncoding checked as the package's Expert table); a program fontTools cannot read is skipped with its error; the programs: every /FontFile3 of subtype Type1C or CIDFontType0C of the pinned pypdf-benchmarks and wild PDFs and of the fetched verapdf-corpus tag (decoded by the pdf package, deduplicated by SHA-256) and fonttools Tests/cffLib/data/TestSupplementEncoding.cff; documents: 38 (38 written, 0 round trips)",
